{
 "_source": "The month under the Live Room's desk: the latest month off each studio's own channel, Ryan's brief of 2026-10-15, in the desk's order. The studios are the ones on the desk, each read off its own channel and never off a channel that collects its recordings. Each channel id was read off the channel's own page (its canonical link and its externalId, which agreed) on 2026-10-15. Filled by tools/pull-live-month.py on the morning timer (tools/daily-live.sh): the latest month of each channel's videos and shorts. Do not hand-edit the log.",
 "_log": "A video is an id, the studio's channel it came from, whether it is long-form or a short, its title as written, when it was published, its state (screen, door, pending or gone), why if it is a door, how long it runs, and its channel's name as YouTube gives it. Nothing else: no description, no thumbnail, no count of any kind, and not where it was played, because nothing on a watch page says and nobody here has looked. The desk is where that is checked.",
